# hidden = globalThis[name]; process[key] = 1; Object.defineProperty semantics: hidden[key] defined as a closure; delete hidden[key]; process.release
# `globalThis[name]` answers the unknown object, and beside it the operand lists `process`. The store under a key nobody knows leaves no member of `process` locked, so the definition and the deletion work at run time:
